                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_the_model_structure_on_cochain_dgcalgebras"} Relation to the model structure on cochain dgc-algebras
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial objects
            in unital,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on commutative non-negative cochain dg-algebras
          %h2#the_model_structure The model structure
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          #CosimplicalCommutativeAlgebras.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cAlg_k^\Delta
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial objects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of unital,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          #ComparisonFunctors.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Sending
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} algebras
              to their underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              yields a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \colon cAlg_k^\Delta \longrightarrow k Mod^\Delta
            %p
              from cosimplicial
              = succeed "-allgebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CosimplicalCommutativeAlgebras"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial objects
              in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %p
              Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              provides the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+cochain+complex"} normalized cochain complex
              functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ch
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N \colon k Mod_k^\Delta \to Ch^{\geq 0}(k)
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complexes"} cochain complexes
              (i.e. with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              of degree +1) in non-negative degrees.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Say that morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cAlg_k^{\Delta}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CosimplicalCommutativeAlgebras"}
            %ol
              %li
                a
                %em weak equivalence
                if its image
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(U(f)) \colon N(U(A)) \to N(U(B))
                under the comparison functors from remark
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonFunctors"}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ch
                          %mrow
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch^{\geq 0}(k)
            %p
              1.a
              %em fibration
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              (i.e. degreewise a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
            %p Then
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  this defines a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                  structure, to be called the
                  %em projective model structure
                  on comsimplicial commutative
                  = succeed "-algebras." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi cAlg
                            %mi k
                            %mi Δ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi poj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cAlg_k^\Delta)_{poj}
              %li
                %p
                  this is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              %li
                %p
                  and a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          %p
            e.g.
            %a{:href => "#Toen00"} Toën 00, theorem 2.1.2
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The first two statements follow by observing that
              = succeed "the" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi cAlg
                        %mi k
                        %mi Δ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi proj
                      %mi is
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cAlg_k^{\Delta})_{proj} is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \circ N
              from remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonFunctors"}
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} projective model structure on chain complexes
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "transferred+model+structure#SufficientConditions"} this prop.
            %p
              The third statement is the content of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialModelStructure"}
              below.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#simplicial_model_category_structure Simplicial model category structure
          %p
            There is also the structure of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi cAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cAlg_k^\Delta
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#cAlgDelta"}
          #cAlgDelta.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Alg_k^{\Delta}
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^X  \in Alg_k^\Delta
              be the corresponding
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochains+on+simplicial+sets"} cochains on simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A^X \;\colon\; [n]  \mapsto (A_n)^{X_n} = \underset{X_n}{\prod} A_n
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              If we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X) \coloneqq Hom_{Set}(X_\bullet,k)
              for the cosimplicial algebra of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochains+on+simplicial+sets"} cochains on simplicial sets
              then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              degreewise finite this may be written as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A^X = A \otimes C(X)
            %p
              where the tensor product is the degreewise tensor product of
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CastiglioniCortinas03"} Castiglioni-Cortinas 03, p. 10
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in Alg_k^\Delta
              define the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_k^\Delta(A,B)
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alg_k^\Delta(A,B) \coloneqq Hom_{sSet}(A, B^{\Delta[\bullet]})
                    \= Hom_{sSet}(A, B \otimes C(\Delta[\bullet]))
                    \\in sSet
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in Alg_k
              regarded as a constant cosimplicial object under the canonical embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_k \hookrightarrow Alg_k^\Delta
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alg_k^\Delta(A, B^{\Delta[n]})
                    \=
                    Alg_k^\Delta(A, B \otimes C(\Delta[n]))
                    \\simeq
                    Alg_k(A_n,B)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B \otimes C(\Delta[n])
              be a morphism of cosimplicial algebras and write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_n : A_n \to B
            %p
              for the component of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              with values in the copy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = B \otimes k
              of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              on the unique non-degenerate
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              coface maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ←
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\Delta[n])_n \leftarrow C(\Delta[n])_{n-1}
              obtained as the pullback of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              face inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n-1] \to \Delta[n]
              restrict on the non-degenerate
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              projections
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ←
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leftarrow k^{n+1} : p_i
            %p
              Accordingly, from the naturality squares for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_n &amp;\stackrel{f_n}{\to}&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{\delta_i}} &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{\mathrlap{p_i}}
                    \\\
                    A_{n-1} &amp;\stackrel{f_{n-1}}{\to}&amp; B^{n+1}
                    }
            %p the bottom horizontal morphism is fixed to have components
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{n-1} = (f_n \circ \delta_0, \cdots, f_n \circ \delta_n)
            %p in the functions on the non-degenerate simplices.
            %p
              By analogous reasoning this fixes all the components of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in all lower degrees with values in the functions on degenerate simplices.
          %p
            The above
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enrichment
            makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi cAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cAlg_k^\Delta
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensored
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} cotensored
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %p And this is compatible with the model category structure:
          #SimplicialModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              With the definitions as above,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cAlg_k^\Delta)_{proj}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Toen00"} Toën 00, theorem 2.1.2
          %h3#relation_to_the_model_structure_on_cochain_dgcalgebras Relation to the model structure on cochain dgc-algebras
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            this is related to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on commutative non-negative cochain dg-algebras
          %h2#references References
          %p Details are in
          %ul
            %li#Toen00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              , section 2.1 of
              %em Affine stacks (Champs affines)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0012219"}> arXiv:math/0012219
              ) .
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"} Rick Jardine
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
          %p The generalization to arbitrary cosimplicial rings is proposition 9.2 of
          %ul
            %li#CastiglioniCortinas03
              J.L. Castiglioni G. Cortiñas,
              %em Cosimplicial versus DG-rings: a version of the Dold-Kan correspondence
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306289"}> arXiv:math/0306289
              )
          %p
            There also aspects of relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
            is discussed. (See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            for more on this).
